From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xinput: Keep Sony hotplug discovery independent of speaker readiness.

Castlevania's automatic Sony fallback opened a replacement Edge in slot zero,
but processed one input report every three seconds while the HID bus kept
delivering reports. There was no native takeover in the game process.

Empty XInput slots are re-enumerated by both the game and Steam's polling
thread. SetupAPI's Sony speaker wait runs under xinput_cs in this path,
blocking the HID reader along with other discovery calls. Use cfgmgr32's
present interface list, as DirectInput already does: XInput needs device paths
and has no dependency on the native speaker endpoint ordering.

Preserve virtual Steam device priority, Sony ownership checks and explicit
device overrides. Treat a missing interface class as an empty list so a fresh
prefix without WINEXINPUT devices still reaches automatic Sony discovery.
Update imports for all four DLLs which compile the shared implementation.

Also release sechost's speaker ordering gate when its bounded wait ends.
On timeout it previously closed an unsignalled event after notification
dispatch. Concurrent enumerators could keep that named object alive and
repeat the timeout indefinitely. Releasing the gate ends the ordering wait;
it does not publish or claim the existence of a speaker endpoint. Keep the
normal native HID/speaker ordering otherwise unchanged.
---
diff --git a/dlls/sechost/service.c b/dlls/sechost/service.c
index 320a28d2a910b2c8e5bdd109cb2cc3a5e55f10ce..5d43ef988a3f5fa6f2e9e20575f76460148fdb4b 100644
--- a/dlls/sechost/service.c
+++ b/dlls/sechost/service.c
@@ -2262,6 +2262,10 @@ static DWORD WINAPI pending_sony_hid_proc( void *arg )
 
     wait = WaitForSingleObject( pending->ready_event, 3000 );
 
+    /* The gate is released even when no speaker was published. Enumerators
+     * can keep the named event alive after this worker closes its handle. */
+    SetEvent( pending->ready_event );
+
     AcquireSRWLockExclusive( &pending_sony_hid_lock );
     dispatch = !pending->cancelled;
     ReleaseSRWLockExclusive( &pending_sony_hid_lock );
